"""herd-board-serve: the herd's state for the reMarkable's Cyber Times (tools/herd-board), over HTTP.

  herd-board-serve [HOST] [PORT]   GET /herd.json[?since=V]: {"v", "at", "edition", "day", "agents": [{name, status,
                                   task, said, section, recent}]}, the ones that need the owner first; "at" is when it last
                                   changed. With since, it holds the request until the herd differs from V, or HOLD
                                   seconds pass (a long poll). Default 127.0.0.1:8791.
  GET /thread.json?pane=P[&since=V]: {"v", "desks": [{name, pane, status}], "name", "status", "items": [{who, text,
                                   at}]}: the desks to choose from and the conversation with one (the last THREAD
                                   turns: what the owner said, and what the agent last wrote before the next), a long
                                   poll as herd.json's. For Correspondence (ui/letters.qml).

Before noon it is the morning edition and each Claude Code agent's section is its work yesterday; after, today's so
far. A section ({"headline", "body"}) is written by Gemini (MODEL, key in KEYF) from what the owner asked and what the
agent wrote back that day, never tool calls or their output: today's again at most every WRITE seconds once there is
more, a past day's once (kept in CACHE). The day's log goes from its start, so each rewrite begins as the last did and
Gemini's implicit cache can bill that part cheaper. Every request is a line in GEMINI/calls.log (tokens and status,
never text), as herd-voice's and herd-summarise's are; a 429 holds all three off Gemini for its retry delay. Everything else is read-only: `herdr agent list` every POLL seconds, and the
agents' session transcripts. recent is an agent's last few exchanges, [{"asked", "replied"}], once its transcript
has been read for a section.
"""
